;; spec:   stdlib §4.3 (row abs), §4.10 (row Math/abs), §4.3 (row Long/MIN_VALUE)
;; expect: trap
;; trap:   integer overflow in neg at i64
;; roots:  ../../lib
;; covers: Math/abs Long/MIN_VALUE
;; Java's Math.abs(Long.MIN_VALUE) is Long.MIN_VALUE, silently negative; here the magnitude of the
;; smallest i64 does not fit an i64 and the call traps (stdlib §4.3: "traps on the minimum of an
;; integer type"). The constant is the smallest i64, so this is the edge of case 654's range.
(ns main (:use fib.core) (:require [Long :as Long] [Math :as Math]))

(defun main () -> i64
  (Math/abs Long/MIN_VALUE))
